1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,010
Characters, actions, places, occupations, and events in this series are fictional and created for entertainment purposes only.

2
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:10,616
They are not intended to urge or promote any behavior in the series.

3
00:00:10,616 --> 00:00:13,199
Viewer discretion is advised.

4
00:00:14,311 --> 00:00:15,662
(Did you know)

5
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:17,408
(that Halley’s Comet)

6
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:20,987
(has an orbital period of about 76 years?)

7
00:00:22,099 --> 00:00:23,571
(I’ve never seen it.)

8
00:00:23,954 --> 00:00:25,001
(I wasn’t born yet.)

9
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,563
(But someone told me that)

10
00:00:28,745 --> 00:00:30,606
(in 30-plus years,)

11
00:00:33,923 --> 00:00:35,574
(it’ll return.)

12
00:00:39,274 --> 00:00:42,060
(I haven’t seen all my friends together
in almost three years.)

13
00:00:42,424 --> 00:00:44,875
(Thara is a lawyer now.)

14
00:00:44,875 --> 00:00:46,231
Why do you keep spinning it?

15
00:00:46,231 --> 00:00:49,211
- Well, otherwise, you'll eat it all.
- (Pok has his own songs.)

16
00:00:49,211 --> 00:00:49,906
Oh, come on.

17
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:52,454
(As for Hem…)

18
00:00:52,454 --> 00:00:53,835
Do you guys think

19
00:00:53,835 --> 00:00:55,200
- (He’s gone off the rails.)
- I should dye my hair blond?

20
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,574
You’ve been saying
you’d dye your hair blond

21
00:00:56,574 --> 00:00:57,743
since we were in school.

22
00:00:57,743 --> 00:00:59,207
I still haven’t seen you do it.

23
00:00:59,207 --> 00:01:00,726
Can you guys stop arguing already?

24
00:01:00,726 --> 00:01:01,958
My friend Cheewa is here.

25
00:01:05,838 --> 00:01:08,073
(And that’s Parncheewa.)

26
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:10,668
(He’s the one who said)

27
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:12,243
It’s gravity.

28
00:01:13,355 --> 00:01:14,430
(the comet)

29
00:01:17,419 --> 00:01:19,312
(will return in 35 years.)

30
00:02:26,209 --> 00:02:28,387
You really like these old songbooks, huh?

31
00:02:28,624 --> 00:02:30,083
No one uses them anymore, dude.

32
00:02:30,630 --> 00:02:33,114
Do you think I should dye my hair blond?

33
00:02:33,114 --> 00:02:36,052
I’d look so cool playing guitar.

34
00:02:36,618 --> 00:02:37,432
Hmm…

35
00:02:38,070 --> 00:02:39,239
Before you get to be cool,

36
00:02:39,239 --> 00:02:41,323
you’ll be making a trip to the discipline office.

37
00:02:41,505 --> 00:02:42,898
Suchart won’t let you graduate.

38
00:02:43,633 --> 00:02:44,583
What the hell?

39
00:02:44,729 --> 00:02:47,547
Why does the school have to get in the way
of my journey as a musician?

40
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:50,799
Don’t they want a cool guitarist
as an alumnus?

41
00:02:50,799 --> 00:02:51,837
Oh.

42
00:02:55,191 --> 00:02:55,962
What’s going on here?

43
00:02:58,878 --> 00:02:59,901
Is he hibernating or something?

44
00:03:01,286 --> 00:03:02,379
Seriously.

45
00:03:02,488 --> 00:03:04,289
You have your own club to sleep in.

46
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:06,870
This is the Music Club.

47
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,155
Why are you sleeping here?

48
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:12,299
Yeah,

49
00:03:12,773 --> 00:03:14,950
Thara is going to think
we locked you up again.

50
00:03:15,533 --> 00:03:19,136
We’re good-looking musicians.

51
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,255
We’re tiny.

52
00:03:20,255 --> 00:03:21,848
How could we lock athletes
like you guys up?

53
00:03:22,249 --> 00:03:22,944
Mm.

54
00:03:23,454 --> 00:03:24,405
You’re giants.

55
00:03:24,405 --> 00:03:27,249
If you threw us, we'd break our bones.

56
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,208
What’s wrong?

57
00:03:30,336 --> 00:03:32,394
Why’s your face all scrunched up like that?

58
00:03:32,759 --> 00:03:33,465
What are you upset about?

59
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:34,789
Did you fight with your dad?

60
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,540
Have you been busy with school?

61
00:04:02,144 --> 00:04:03,156
Same as usual.

62
00:04:03,903 --> 00:04:06,587
Coach Ong called me yesterday.

63
00:04:06,587 --> 00:04:07,754
He said you missed practice.

64
00:04:15,929 --> 00:04:17,518
I had a headache,
so I went to rest in the nurse’s office.

65
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,185
You looked fine
when you came home yesterday.

66
00:04:24,062 --> 00:04:26,295
How did you have a headache?

67
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:32,683
You need to be more responsible.

68
00:04:34,779 --> 00:04:36,247
Go to practice regularly.

69
00:04:37,815 --> 00:04:39,209
You’re a grown-up now.

70
00:04:39,464 --> 00:04:41,145
I don’t want to keep nagging you.

71
00:04:48,916 --> 00:04:49,416
Okay.

72
00:04:54,082 --> 00:04:56,026
You guys seriously want to be musicians?

73
00:04:56,846 --> 00:04:58,029
I see you guys practicing every day.

74
00:04:59,761 --> 00:05:00,454
Come on.

75
00:05:00,910 --> 00:05:02,177
What kind of question is that?

76
00:05:02,505 --> 00:05:03,367
Of course we do.

77
00:05:03,932 --> 00:05:05,983
We only have one dream.

78
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:07,605
Just you wait.

79
00:05:07,605 --> 00:05:12,986
Once I graduate, I’m going to put out a tape
that’ll be playing everywhere.

80
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:14,028
Yeah.

81
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:16,563
I’m going to put out a tape as a real artist.

82
00:05:17,037 --> 00:05:19,301
Corporate jobs

83
00:05:19,301 --> 00:05:20,760
aren’t our thing.

84
00:05:21,143 --> 00:05:22,554
Just so you know,

85
00:05:23,064 --> 00:05:26,533
no one makes tapes anymore, Mr. Hemaraj.

86
00:05:27,153 --> 00:05:28,189
Well, I like them.

87
00:05:28,317 --> 00:05:29,011
Oh.

88
00:05:29,011 --> 00:05:30,746
We still have a few years
before we graduate.

89
00:05:31,365 --> 00:05:32,915
How did you guys figure yourselves out
so fast?

90
00:05:34,319 --> 00:05:37,457
I don’t know if I’ll really become a singer
in the future,

91
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:41,476
but it’s what I like now, so I keep practicing.

92
00:05:42,314 --> 00:05:43,834
Just like you practice judo.

93
00:05:44,253 --> 00:05:45,308
Isn’t it because you like it?

94
00:05:56,526 --> 00:05:57,368
(Like it?)

95
00:05:58,826 --> 00:06:01,098
(I don’t even know if I really like it.)

96
00:06:04,835 --> 00:06:06,013
He’s hibernating again.

97
00:06:07,581 --> 00:06:10,515
(My life is just like a dark universe.)

98
00:06:12,301 --> 00:06:13,287
(Pitch black.)

99
00:06:14,490 --> 00:06:16,461
(I don’t even know what I like or don’t like.)

100
00:06:17,828 --> 00:06:19,077
(I just live)

101
00:06:20,371 --> 00:06:21,356
(day by day.)

102
00:06:23,890 --> 00:06:25,053
(So ordinary.)

103
00:06:27,988 --> 00:06:29,518
(When it comes to judo,)

104
00:06:31,541 --> 00:06:32,500
(it feels ordinary too.)

105
00:06:33,667 --> 00:06:34,485
(No feeling.)

106
00:06:35,214 --> 00:06:36,078
(No excitement.)

107
00:06:39,359 --> 00:06:40,808
(I’m just Niran.)

108
00:06:44,447 --> 00:06:45,721
(Nothing special.)

109
00:06:48,127 --> 00:06:49,457
(That’s why I love coming here.)

110
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,139
(Lying down, listening to the music playing
as they chase their dreams.)

111
00:06:53,777 --> 00:06:57,099
(One day, I’ll probably find my own path.)

112
00:06:57,445 --> 00:06:58,768
Mr. Judo.

113
00:06:58,969 --> 00:07:00,389
I knew you’d be here.

114
00:07:00,991 --> 00:07:01,728
Again.

115
00:07:01,728 --> 00:07:04,001
(Ugh, the judo guy is asking for me.)

116
00:07:04,001 --> 00:07:05,564
Coach asked me to come get you.

117
00:07:05,983 --> 00:07:08,059
Ugh!

118
00:07:09,635 --> 00:07:10,400
Let’s go.

119
00:07:10,815 --> 00:07:11,315
Help me.

120
00:07:13,393 --> 00:07:14,480
I had nothing to do with it.

121
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:15,825
I didn’t lock him up.

122
00:07:15,825 --> 00:07:17,326
I didn’t ask him to come here.

123
00:07:17,691 --> 00:07:18,687
Bye-bye.

124
00:07:21,075 --> 00:07:22,216
What did I tell you?

125
00:07:23,146 --> 00:07:25,186
If you have a problem, come and tell me.

126
00:07:25,842 --> 00:07:27,064
Don’t disappear like that.

127
00:07:28,850 --> 00:07:29,773
I’m sorry, Coach.

128
00:07:29,773 --> 00:07:30,770
I forgot the time.

129
00:07:33,049 --> 00:07:34,834
Why didn’t you remind your friend, Thara?

130
00:07:35,855 --> 00:07:36,355
Oh?

131
00:07:39,035 --> 00:07:41,905
Making the national team
doesn’t mean you can skip practice, Niran.

132
00:07:43,217 --> 00:07:44,640
No matter how good you are,

133
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:47,407
you still have to put in the work
and be responsible.

134
00:07:47,589 --> 00:07:51,248
Otherwise, everything you’ve achieved
will slowly fade away.

135
00:07:51,649 --> 00:07:52,613
Come on, Coach.

136
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:54,103
Niran is so talented.

137
00:07:54,322 --> 00:07:56,539
He could keep throwing for the rest of his life.

138
00:07:56,885 --> 00:07:59,778
Athletes lose because they think that way.

139
00:08:00,106 --> 00:08:00,787
Oh.

140
00:08:01,735 --> 00:08:02,986
I’m warning you

141
00:08:02,986 --> 00:08:04,146
because I mean well.

142
00:08:04,765 --> 00:08:06,234
If you really have any problems,

143
00:08:06,234 --> 00:08:07,720
we can talk about them.

144
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:08,695
Got it, Niran?

145
00:08:11,903 --> 00:08:12,910
Yes, Coach.

146
00:08:50,521 --> 00:08:51,889
Coach must be mad at me.

147
00:08:52,928 --> 00:08:55,260
For skipping practice or losing to Most?

148
00:08:55,661 --> 00:08:56,638
Both.

149
00:08:56,948 --> 00:08:57,943
Coach Ong can never be mad at you.

150
00:08:58,508 --> 00:08:59,653
He loves you so much.

151
00:09:00,473 --> 00:09:02,399
But what’s going on?

152
00:09:02,928 --> 00:09:04,346
Why did you let Most throw you like that?

153
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,680
Did he cheat?

154
00:09:06,788 --> 00:09:07,646
Do you want me to tell Coach?

155
00:09:08,375 --> 00:09:09,847
Most is just really good.

156
00:09:09,847 --> 00:09:10,814
Better than you?

157
00:09:11,361 --> 00:09:12,322
That’s impossible.

158
00:09:13,106 --> 00:09:14,043
It’s possible.

159
00:09:14,535 --> 00:09:15,821
Everyone is better than me.

160
00:09:16,386 --> 00:09:17,354
Except you.

161
00:09:18,812 --> 00:09:19,625
You brat!

162
00:09:20,263 --> 00:09:21,582
I know how to box.

163
00:09:21,947 --> 00:09:22,631
Really?

164
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:24,885
Is that how you stand?

165
00:09:25,614 --> 00:09:26,653
I don’t think so.

166
00:09:28,072 --> 00:09:29,316
Be for real.

167
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:30,781
I’m going to punch you for real.

168
00:09:30,781 --> 00:09:31,361
Oh!

169
00:09:31,507 --> 00:09:32,644
Don’t run.

170
00:09:32,644 --> 00:09:33,538
You can’t punch me.

171
00:09:33,702 --> 00:09:34,680
Where are you going?

172
00:09:35,245 --> 00:09:36,414
I’m going home.

173
00:09:36,414 --> 00:09:37,859
See you, buddy.
Get home safe.

174
00:09:37,859 --> 00:09:39,456
You can try to punch me tomorrow.

175
00:09:39,456 --> 00:09:40,391
Bye-bye.

176
00:09:42,654 --> 00:09:43,964
Yeah. See you!

177
00:10:24,824 --> 00:10:26,079
Someone from the Boxing Club

178
00:10:26,079 --> 00:10:27,738
walked to the basement of
the science building at night.

179
00:10:27,738 --> 00:10:29,040
Then something dropped on him.

180
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:30,170
It looked just like blood.

181
00:10:31,647 --> 00:10:32,605
What does that mean?

182
00:10:32,605 --> 00:10:33,649
Are you insulting us, four-eyes?

183
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,000
Are you trying to get on my damn nerves?

184
00:10:52,302 --> 00:10:52,802
Oh.

185
00:10:53,435 --> 00:10:54,078
Sorry.

186
00:10:54,078 --> 00:10:54,909
I lost my balance.

187
00:10:58,050 --> 00:10:59,284
It’s gravity.

188
00:11:01,164 --> 00:11:01,837
Huh?

189
00:11:02,352 --> 00:11:03,579
You fell just now

190
00:11:04,133 --> 00:11:05,287
because of gravity.

191
00:11:09,444 --> 00:11:12,489
According to Newton’s law
of universal gravitation,

192
00:11:12,489 --> 00:11:15,279
no matter where you are in the universe,

193
00:11:15,279 --> 00:11:16,948
there’s always a gravitational pull on mass.

194
00:11:16,948 --> 00:11:19,102
The force is proportional
to the product of the masses

195
00:11:19,102 --> 00:11:22,598
and inversely proportional
to the square of the distance between them.

196
00:11:24,576 --> 00:11:25,961
Like right now,

197
00:11:26,317 --> 00:11:28,871
your gravitational force is pressing down
on my books.

198
00:11:29,227 --> 00:11:29,881
Oh.

199
00:11:30,752 --> 00:11:31,252
Sorry.

200
00:11:31,252 --> 00:11:32,002
I didn’t mean it.

201
00:11:32,616 --> 00:11:33,234
COMPLETE SUMMARY OF
HIGH SCHOOL PHYSICS

202
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:36,087
It’s alright. Gravity is normal.

203
00:11:39,668 --> 00:11:40,846
Ah…

204
00:11:41,361 --> 00:11:42,094
Okay.

205
00:11:42,886 --> 00:11:45,149
Without gravity,

206
00:11:46,238 --> 00:11:48,017
we’d all die.

207
00:11:50,202 --> 00:11:51,313
Ah…

208
00:11:51,907 --> 00:11:52,557
Okay.

209
00:12:14,673 --> 00:12:16,136
Do you want to sit down?

210
00:12:19,165 --> 00:12:22,033
Did you know there’ll be a bigger jolt
at the intersection up ahead?

211
00:12:22,033 --> 00:12:22,791
What’s that?

212
00:12:23,088 --> 00:12:24,005
It’s—

213
00:12:27,623 --> 00:12:28,816
It's a jolt.

214
00:12:29,489 --> 00:12:30,624
We just went through one.

215
00:12:30,624 --> 00:12:31,760
You’re safe now.

216
00:12:38,578 --> 00:12:40,961
♪ Wanna be loved ♪

217
00:12:41,258 --> 00:12:42,433
No, Thipok.

218
00:12:42,433 --> 00:12:43,853
You sang that line wrong.

219
00:12:44,091 --> 00:12:46,343
I sang it right. It’s about the feel.

220
00:12:46,610 --> 00:12:48,308
I improvised.

221
00:12:48,308 --> 00:12:50,096
Ad-lib, you know?

222
00:12:50,096 --> 00:12:51,106
Ad-lib.

223
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:53,060
If you don’t remember the lyrics,

224
00:12:53,060 --> 00:12:55,037
you can just sing gibberish for now.

225
00:12:55,413 --> 00:12:58,170
Can you really do that? Sing gibberish?

226
00:12:58,170 --> 00:12:59,400
Of course.

227
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:01,320
All the famous singers do it.

228
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:04,041
If you don’t believe me, Pok will show you.

229
00:13:04,041 --> 00:13:06,930
♪ Tua-tua-nga-nga, tua-tua-nga ♪

230
00:13:06,930 --> 00:13:08,385
♪ Tua-nga ♪

231
00:13:08,385 --> 00:13:10,330
♪ Tua-nga, tua-tua ♪

232
00:13:10,330 --> 00:13:11,670
Screw gravity.

233
00:13:11,670 --> 00:13:12,907
Nonsense.

234
00:13:14,850 --> 00:13:17,565
Look, I’m not encouraging him to lip-sync.

235
00:13:17,565 --> 00:13:20,358
He’ll memorize the lyrics tonight.

236
00:13:21,247 --> 00:13:22,395
I’m sorry.

237
00:13:22,771 --> 00:13:24,236
I know you love this song.

238
00:13:24,414 --> 00:13:28,045
I’ll hurry home and memorize the lyrics
word for word, okay?

239
00:13:28,362 --> 00:13:30,563
Or what’s got you so worked up?

240
00:13:31,137 --> 00:13:32,024
Don’t tell me

241
00:13:32,490 --> 00:13:34,050
you’re thinking about when you lost to Most?

242
00:13:34,050 --> 00:13:35,042
Seriously?

243
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:37,016
You lost to Most?

244
00:13:37,155 --> 00:13:38,490
Poor you, buddy.

245
00:13:38,490 --> 00:13:41,169
This is your rock bottom.

246
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,229
Yeah.

247
00:13:44,387 --> 00:13:47,658
That means forgetting the lyrics
isn’t a big deal.

248
00:13:47,658 --> 00:13:48,317
You idiot.

249
00:13:48,416 --> 00:13:49,639
It’s a big deal. Don’t be funny.

250
00:13:50,193 --> 00:13:52,890
It’s just a minor slip-up, not rock bottom.

251
00:13:52,890 --> 00:13:53,807
Right, Niran?

252
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:55,871
I ran all the way here.

253
00:13:56,570 --> 00:13:58,290
Can you guys stop talking about judo?

254
00:13:58,765 --> 00:13:59,530
You guys keep talking about it.

255
00:13:59,530 --> 00:14:00,226
Damn.

256
00:14:02,570 --> 00:14:03,345
What now?

257
00:14:03,464 --> 00:14:04,427
By the way, guys,

258
00:14:04,882 --> 00:14:06,357
have you heard about the ghost
in the science building?

259
00:14:06,909 --> 00:14:09,043
Oh, I think that’s interesting.

260
00:14:09,043 --> 00:14:11,390
I’m sick of hearing about judo too.

261
00:14:11,390 --> 00:14:12,272
Yeah.

262
00:14:13,262 --> 00:14:14,047
Go on.

263
00:14:14,602 --> 00:14:15,314
Well…

264
00:14:16,264 --> 00:14:21,680
They say there's a ghost roaming around
the science building lately.

265
00:14:22,492 --> 00:14:23,368
How?

266
00:14:24,595 --> 00:14:27,162
Someone from the Boxing Club

267
00:14:27,162 --> 00:14:29,108
walked to the basement of
the science building at night.

268
00:14:29,266 --> 00:14:30,716
Then something dropped on him.

269
00:14:31,250 --> 00:14:32,434
It looked just like blood.

270
00:14:33,582 --> 00:14:34,402
Blood?

271
00:14:34,541 --> 00:14:35,683
That must be an exaggeration.

272
00:14:36,277 --> 00:14:37,177
Nonsense.

273
00:14:37,530 --> 00:14:39,450
Why would a ghost be in
the science building?

274
00:14:39,589 --> 00:14:41,765
Why isn’t it at the Thai dance room?

275
00:14:42,062 --> 00:14:43,934
But I think ghosts are everywhere, no?

276
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:49,862
Does that mean
there’s a ghost in this room?

277
00:14:50,674 --> 00:14:54,932
Watch out in your judo practice room
when you two shower late at night.

278
00:14:55,250 --> 00:14:56,345
What did I just tell you?

279
00:14:56,682 --> 00:14:58,122
I didn’t mean it.

280
00:14:58,122 --> 00:14:58,994
It’s Thara’s fault.

281
00:14:58,994 --> 00:15:00,004
He provoked me.

282
00:15:00,696 --> 00:15:01,814
Yeah, whatever.

283
00:15:02,170 --> 00:15:03,409
I don’t know what ghost it is.

284
00:15:03,409 --> 00:15:04,835
Maybe Sir Isaac Newton’s ghost.

285
00:15:05,090 --> 00:15:06,730
If you guys don’t believe me,

286
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:08,921
let’s prove it together

287
00:15:20,230 --> 00:15:21,324
Where’s your ghost?

288
00:15:21,641 --> 00:15:24,167
Look, there’s a whole bunch of us here.

289
00:15:24,405 --> 00:15:25,842
If I were that ghost, I’d be scared.

290
00:15:26,179 --> 00:15:27,495
Especially with Niran here.

291
00:15:28,771 --> 00:15:31,101
The ghost must be scared of
getting thrown to the ground.

292
00:15:32,249 --> 00:15:33,633
Want me to throw you?

293
00:15:33,871 --> 00:15:35,553
Hey, look.

294
00:15:38,542 --> 00:15:40,286
Astronomy Club.

295
00:15:42,859 --> 00:15:44,786
It’s on the top floor.

296
00:15:45,657 --> 00:15:46,618
They say

297
00:15:46,618 --> 00:15:49,198
the higher, the weirder.

298
00:15:49,614 --> 00:15:50,400
This building is like that.

299
00:15:52,149 --> 00:15:53,321
I think you’re the weird one.

300
00:15:53,855 --> 00:15:54,913
Excuse me?

301
00:16:01,168 --> 00:16:02,346
See you guys later.

302
00:16:02,683 --> 00:16:04,003
Do your best at practice.

303
00:16:04,161 --> 00:16:05,283
Good luck.

304
00:16:05,402 --> 00:16:06,846
Don’t lose to Most again.

305
00:16:07,064 --> 00:16:08,273
I don’t like his face.

306
00:16:08,669 --> 00:16:09,504
Most’s face?

307
00:16:09,951 --> 00:16:10,576
Your face.

308
00:16:11,724 --> 00:16:13,006
You two just go.

309
00:16:13,976 --> 00:16:14,759
- See you.
- See you.

310
00:16:15,135 --> 00:16:15,788
Bye.

311
00:16:21,607 --> 00:16:22,708
You go to practice.

312
00:16:22,708 --> 00:16:23,681
I’m skipping.

313
00:16:23,879 --> 00:16:24,594
What?

314
00:16:24,594 --> 00:16:25,516
You’re skipping again?

315
00:16:25,635 --> 00:16:26,170
Why?

316
00:16:28,050 --> 00:16:28,822
I’m lazy.

317
00:16:28,822 --> 00:16:29,748
You should go.

318
00:16:30,370 --> 00:16:31,152
Just go.

319
00:16:31,152 --> 00:16:32,209
I’m gonna hurry home.

320
00:16:36,544 --> 00:16:37,221
See you.

321
00:16:45,769 --> 00:16:47,587
I really am out of money.

322
00:16:48,201 --> 00:16:51,010
I spent all my allowance on stuff for the club.

323
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:51,836
How am I supposed to know?

324
00:16:52,746 --> 00:16:53,951
You’re supposed to know

325
00:16:54,050 --> 00:16:56,210
you have to pay for our dinner.

326
00:16:56,408 --> 00:16:58,194
Can’t you even manage your money?

327
00:16:58,926 --> 00:16:59,919
I’m sorry.

328
00:17:00,157 --> 00:17:02,059
No way he’s spent it all. He’s lying.

329
00:17:03,583 --> 00:17:04,723
I’m telling the truth.

330
00:17:04,921 --> 00:17:10,646
Lying to you guys in this situation
would only make things worse for me.

331
00:17:10,903 --> 00:17:11,558
What does that mean?

332
00:17:11,558 --> 00:17:12,758
Are you insulting us, four-eyes?

333
00:17:13,970 --> 00:17:15,114
No.

334
00:17:15,510 --> 00:17:18,239
I’m just judging the probability
based on your personalities.

335
00:17:18,378 --> 00:17:20,093
If you two change your personalities,

336
00:17:20,350 --> 00:17:22,008
I’ll analyze it differently.

337
00:17:22,008 --> 00:17:24,173
Are you trying to get on my damn nerves?

338
00:17:29,354 --> 00:17:30,460
How is this all you have?

339
00:17:31,430 --> 00:17:33,168
Naw, search him.

340
00:17:33,366 --> 00:17:34,466
If there’s more, I’ll take it all.

341
00:17:35,812 --> 00:17:36,712
Hey.

342
00:17:37,009 --> 00:17:39,068
Do people still shake kids down
for money these days?

343
00:17:39,068 --> 00:17:40,268
How much do you want?

344
00:17:40,525 --> 00:17:41,535
I’ll donate it to you.

345
00:17:43,119 --> 00:17:45,733
What the hell does someone from
the Judo Club like you have to do with this?

346
00:17:46,386 --> 00:17:48,472
And does someone from the Boxing Club
like you not have money to eat?

347
00:17:48,472 --> 00:17:49,780
Is that why you have to take it
from someone else?

348
00:17:51,090 --> 00:17:52,544
Go ask your mom for it.

349
00:17:53,435 --> 00:17:54,827
Are you trying to get on my nerves?

350
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:56,893
How about I kick your ass first?

351
00:17:57,348 --> 00:17:57,934
Wait.

352
00:17:59,825 --> 00:18:00,969
Hey…

353
00:18:02,077 --> 00:18:03,243
Gravity Junior.

354
00:18:08,014 --> 00:18:08,605
Run.

355
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:33,692
Hey.

356
00:18:34,207 --> 00:18:35,193
I think they went that way.

357
00:18:36,005 --> 00:18:36,665
Come on.

358
00:18:43,534 --> 00:18:44,429
Idiots.

359
00:18:44,864 --> 00:18:46,381
Blind as hell.

360
00:18:50,142 --> 00:18:50,925
Niran!

361
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:52,210
Niran!

362
00:18:52,428 --> 00:18:53,629
Wake up, man.

363
00:18:53,629 --> 00:18:55,383
Those two already left.

364
00:18:57,501 --> 00:18:59,917
Are you sleeping for the world championship
or what?

365
00:19:02,648 --> 00:19:03,410
Come on.

366
00:19:03,410 --> 00:19:04,649
Let’s go, man.

367
00:19:04,649 --> 00:19:06,012
I’m hungry.

368
00:19:06,349 --> 00:19:07,024
Ugh!

369
00:19:07,222 --> 00:19:09,695
You’re never awake during brainy classes.

370
00:19:14,842 --> 00:19:16,034
Hi, Auntie Tang.

371
00:19:16,272 --> 00:19:17,846
Hi, Niran.

372
00:19:18,044 --> 00:19:21,286
Your dad told me
you don’t really finish your breakfast.

373
00:19:21,286 --> 00:19:22,810
I don’t really have an appetite in the morning.

374
00:19:22,810 --> 00:19:23,902
I wake up late too.

375
00:19:23,902 --> 00:19:26,036
So I figured I’d just get lunch from you.

376
00:19:26,036 --> 00:19:28,807
You can try other places too.

377
00:19:28,807 --> 00:19:31,337
I know we’re relatives,
but you don’t have to keep eating my food.

378
00:19:31,337 --> 00:19:32,995
I’m not eating it because we’re relatives,

379
00:19:32,995 --> 00:19:33,947
but because it’s good.

380
00:19:34,422 --> 00:19:36,927
Your food tastes comforting.

381
00:19:37,482 --> 00:19:39,502
It feels like home.

382
00:19:40,050 --> 00:19:43,350
Today, can I get
stir-fried vegetables and…

383
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:44,132
clear soup?

384
00:19:44,132 --> 00:19:44,988
Let’s get you some meat.

385
00:19:44,988 --> 00:19:45,948
Fried chicken?

386
00:19:45,948 --> 00:19:49,165
Can I also get this, this, this,
and the chicken curry too?

387
00:19:49,165 --> 00:19:49,888
Sure.

388
00:19:51,254 --> 00:19:51,957
Hem!

389
00:19:52,175 --> 00:19:53,374
Go get in line properly.

390
00:19:53,512 --> 00:19:54,304
Come on.

391
00:19:54,423 --> 00:19:56,264
I have you get food for me every day.

392
00:19:56,264 --> 00:19:57,391
This time, I just ordered it myself.

393
00:19:57,885 --> 00:19:59,370
Someone could yell at us!

394
00:19:59,370 --> 00:20:00,169
I won’t.

395
00:20:01,554 --> 00:20:02,492
See?

396
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:05,685
This kid is so generous.

397
00:20:05,685 --> 00:20:06,464
What’s your name?

398
00:20:06,464 --> 00:20:08,349
I’ll remember it.

399
00:20:08,626 --> 00:20:10,828
Next time you want to order,
just ask me to do it for you.

400
00:20:11,066 --> 00:20:12,140
You’re…

401
00:20:12,892 --> 00:20:14,468
Parncheeaa.

402
00:20:15,181 --> 00:20:16,256
It’s Parncheewa.

403
00:20:16,429 --> 00:20:17,358
Parncheewa.

404
00:20:17,383 --> 00:20:17,923
Right.

405
00:20:18,061 --> 00:20:19,268
Cute with glasses.

406
00:20:19,268 --> 00:20:20,608
My dear little brother.

407
00:20:23,003 --> 00:20:24,086
Please give me a big portion.

408
00:20:24,086 --> 00:20:24,878
I’m hungry.

409
00:20:24,877 --> 00:20:25,847
Sure.

410
00:20:26,718 --> 00:20:27,801
You’re really not mad?

411
00:20:29,563 --> 00:20:30,621
No, I’m not.

412
00:20:31,037 --> 00:20:32,397
You saved me yesterday.

413
00:20:32,397 --> 00:20:33,862
I’m not going to get mad over
something this small.

414
00:20:36,949 --> 00:20:38,050
Your food is ready.

415
00:20:38,783 --> 00:20:40,075
Here you go. Extra portion for you.

416
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:42,898
Thank you, Auntie Tang.

417
00:20:46,050 --> 00:20:47,381
Hem, grab me a spoon and fork.

418
00:20:47,381 --> 00:20:48,214
Ugh!

419
00:20:50,094 --> 00:20:51,114
The usual, please.

420
00:20:51,114 --> 00:20:51,895
Alright.

421
00:21:00,738 --> 00:21:01,470
Oh?

422
00:21:01,668 --> 00:21:03,122
I thought you said you were getting noodles.

423
00:21:03,122 --> 00:21:06,240
I walked past Niran
and saw him ordering from Auntie Tang.

424
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:09,090
It looked so good, so I went there too.

425
00:21:09,090 --> 00:21:10,463
I bet you cut the line.

426
00:21:10,542 --> 00:21:11,170
Right, Niran?

427
00:21:11,170 --> 00:21:12,165
Obviously.

428
00:21:12,165 --> 00:21:13,432
Hey!

429
00:21:13,432 --> 00:21:14,573
Watch what you say.

430
00:21:14,850 --> 00:21:16,503
I already asked the kid behind us.

431
00:21:16,610 --> 00:21:17,827
He was okay with it.

432
00:21:17,827 --> 00:21:19,316
I don’t know if he wanted to punch me, though.

433
00:21:19,415 --> 00:21:20,922
He had such a poker face,

434
00:21:21,239 --> 00:21:22,518
even though he’s kind of timid.

435
00:21:22,973 --> 00:21:24,299
His name is…

436
00:21:24,490 --> 00:21:26,266
Parngmeena.

437
00:21:26,266 --> 00:21:27,286
Parncheewa.

438
00:21:27,530 --> 00:21:28,161
Yeah.

439
00:21:28,161 --> 00:21:29,096
Parncheewa.

440
00:21:29,096 --> 00:21:30,446
Parncheewa?

441
00:21:30,446 --> 00:21:31,448
Grade 11.

442
00:21:32,339 --> 00:21:33,641
Student council member?

443
00:21:33,641 --> 00:21:35,426
I don’t know if he’s on the student council,

444
00:21:36,198 --> 00:21:37,410
but I think he’s an 11th grader.

445
00:21:37,410 --> 00:21:39,103
I think I used to see him around.

446
00:21:39,610 --> 00:21:41,717
He took drum classes at my dad’s school.

447
00:21:41,891 --> 00:21:43,161
He’s no joke.

448
00:21:44,091 --> 00:21:46,343
But he’s kind of nerdy.

449
00:21:46,521 --> 00:21:48,437
He probably doesn’t play anymore.

450
00:21:49,130 --> 00:21:50,423
What a cool kid.

451
00:21:51,175 --> 00:21:53,472
Hey, should we invite him to join our band?

452
00:21:54,264 --> 00:21:55,628
He’s on the student council.

453
00:21:57,786 --> 00:21:59,870
And he’s in Teacher Boriboon’s club.

454
00:22:01,117 --> 00:22:02,155
Standout.

455
00:22:02,709 --> 00:22:04,070
Extracurricular kid.

456
00:22:04,070 --> 00:22:05,149
Top student.

457
00:22:05,446 --> 00:22:06,669
Most importantly,

458
00:22:07,283 --> 00:22:08,619
he’s freaking handsome.

459
00:22:09,629 --> 00:22:13,218
In that nerdy, glasses-wearing kind of way.

460
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:26,695
You forgot this at the food stall.

461
00:22:44,843 --> 00:22:46,872
Damn. He’s really handsome.

462
00:22:50,831 --> 00:22:52,318
The nerdy, handsome type with glasses.

463
00:22:53,842 --> 00:22:57,477
Is my friend seriously having a lollipop
before food?

464
00:22:58,050 --> 00:22:58,938
What?

465
00:22:58,938 --> 00:22:59,759
Did you do it?

466
00:22:59,759 --> 00:23:00,965
Why did you tell Suchart?

467
00:23:00,965 --> 00:23:02,018
I didn’t want you to get hurt.

468
00:23:02,018 --> 00:23:03,904
Why do you keep
meddling in my business?

469
00:23:03,904 --> 00:23:04,798
You call this meddling?

470
00:23:04,798 --> 00:23:06,313
You know Cheewa?

471
00:23:06,313 --> 00:23:07,019
Are you guys close?

472
00:23:07,019 --> 00:23:07,805
That kid with the glasses?

473
00:23:19,715 --> 00:23:20,345
Yo!

474
00:23:21,620 --> 00:23:22,698
We’re running late today.

475
00:23:23,102 --> 00:23:24,221
Have you had breakfast?

476
00:23:24,495 --> 00:23:25,387
No.

477
00:23:25,387 --> 00:23:26,394
I woke up late too.

478
00:23:26,733 --> 00:23:27,533
Seriously?

479
00:23:28,001 --> 00:23:29,747
You have someone
making you breakfast every day,

480
00:23:29,989 --> 00:23:31,301
and you still couldn’t wake up in time
to eat it?

481
00:23:32,770 --> 00:23:33,983
I get tired of that too.

482
00:23:35,016 --> 00:23:35,872
How?

483
00:23:36,114 --> 00:23:38,000
Isn’t it your dad who cooks for you?

484
00:23:38,210 --> 00:23:39,704
Or your Auntie Tang?

485
00:23:40,527 --> 00:23:42,557
Did you guys see the school group chat?

486
00:23:42,654 --> 00:23:45,484
Someone said they saw cockroaches
at Auntie Tang’s food stall.

487
00:23:45,904 --> 00:23:47,228
Everyone’s bashing her.

488
00:23:47,389 --> 00:23:49,031
They said they’re not buying food
from her anymore.

489
00:23:52,647 --> 00:23:54,539
Not selling much today?

490
00:23:55,362 --> 00:23:58,237
I’ve only sold two today.

491
00:23:58,754 --> 00:24:01,719
Lunch break is almost over.

492
00:24:01,880 --> 00:24:04,763
I don’t know why no one came by.

493
00:24:04,973 --> 00:24:07,861
I think my food tastes the same as always.

494
00:24:14,254 --> 00:24:15,199
Was it you?

495
00:24:17,556 --> 00:24:18,249
What?

496
00:24:18,249 --> 00:24:18,993
Did you do it?

497
00:24:19,962 --> 00:24:20,744
What’s wrong with you?

498
00:24:22,035 --> 00:24:22,886
Where’s your proof?

499
00:24:22,886 --> 00:24:23,577
What did I do?

500
00:24:23,577 --> 00:24:24,564
The proof is all over your face.

501
00:24:24,564 --> 00:24:25,064
Hey.

502
00:24:26,727 --> 00:24:27,759
If you’re mad at me, take it out on me.

503
00:24:27,759 --> 00:24:28,528
It’s my business.

504
00:24:28,528 --> 00:24:29,494
Why did you take it out on her?

505
00:24:29,494 --> 00:24:30,461
What the hell does she have to do with this?

506
00:24:31,058 --> 00:24:32,504
And what did you have to do with it yesterday?

507
00:24:33,210 --> 00:24:33,953
Niran.

508
00:24:34,276 --> 00:24:36,071
Don’t. It’s not worth it.

509
00:24:36,765 --> 00:24:39,475
You should listen to your friend.

510
00:24:39,846 --> 00:24:42,434
You’re only as tall as my friend’s knee.

511
00:24:42,434 --> 00:24:43,535
His knee, my ass!

512
00:24:44,471 --> 00:24:45,071
You jerk!

513
00:24:45,814 --> 00:24:47,118
Stay the f*ck out of this!

514
00:24:47,409 --> 00:24:47,909
Hey!

515
00:24:48,522 --> 00:24:49,530
Stop it right now!

516
00:25:01,769 --> 00:25:02,906
What were you thinking?

517
00:25:03,210 --> 00:25:04,944
Fighting in the canteen?

518
00:25:06,300 --> 00:25:09,302
If Cheewa hadn’t run to tell me,

519
00:25:10,028 --> 00:25:12,690
you’d have fought until lunch break was over.

520
00:25:14,853 --> 00:25:17,120
What’s wrong with your two clubs?

521
00:25:17,233 --> 00:25:18,635
Why do you keep fighting?

522
00:25:26,358 --> 00:25:28,099
This time,

523
00:25:28,599 --> 00:25:30,728
I’m deducting your behavior points.

524
00:25:31,390 --> 00:25:35,639
And you’ll have to complete
whatever activities you can

525
00:25:36,365 --> 00:25:38,804
to make up for the points you lose.

526
00:25:40,047 --> 00:25:43,342
Otherwise, you won’t graduate
from high school.

527
00:25:51,314 --> 00:25:51,993
Damn.

528
00:25:52,913 --> 00:25:53,731
It’s all your fault.

529
00:25:54,441 --> 00:25:55,528
You started it.

530
00:25:55,528 --> 00:25:56,630
No, you started it.

531
00:25:57,049 --> 00:25:59,030
Who told you to extort money from people?

532
00:25:59,030 --> 00:25:59,749
Did you not have your own?

533
00:25:59,959 --> 00:26:01,235
I wasn’t bullying you, was I?

534
00:26:02,155 --> 00:26:02,962
But he’s younger.

535
00:26:02,962 --> 00:26:03,559
Please stop.

536
00:26:07,643 --> 00:26:08,274
Let’s go.

537
00:26:12,532 --> 00:26:13,494
Oh, please.

538
00:26:14,140 --> 00:26:15,373
I thought they were tougher than that.

539
00:26:19,635 --> 00:26:20,335
And you.

540
00:26:21,352 --> 00:26:22,723
Why did you tell Suchart?

541
00:26:25,193 --> 00:26:26,672
I was afraid to step in.

542
00:26:26,672 --> 00:26:27,559
I was afraid I’d get caught in the middle.

543
00:26:28,302 --> 00:26:29,232
Why would you step in?

544
00:26:29,910 --> 00:26:31,058
I didn’t want you to get hurt.

545
00:26:32,462 --> 00:26:33,680
I do judo.

546
00:26:33,793 --> 00:26:35,336
You think I can’t fight them?

547
00:26:36,724 --> 00:26:38,863
If I got hurt, I’d only hurt my hand
punching them in the face.

548
00:26:38,863 --> 00:26:40,062
I know you can fight them,

549
00:26:40,191 --> 00:26:41,707
but I don’t want you to get hurt.

550
00:26:42,982 --> 00:26:44,185
Not even your hand.

551
00:27:02,349 --> 00:27:04,889
My club has activities you can do
to earn points.

552
00:27:05,728 --> 00:27:08,925
If you’re interested, come apply.

553
00:27:11,734 --> 00:27:13,363
Mm. I’ll check it out.

554
00:27:15,994 --> 00:27:18,364
Anyway, why do you keep
meddling in my business?

555
00:27:18,671 --> 00:27:19,714
You call this meddling?

556
00:27:20,214 --> 00:27:20,714
Oh?

557
00:27:20,875 --> 00:27:21,638
You’re definitely meddling.

558
00:27:22,074 --> 00:27:23,112
It’s not even your business.

559
00:27:24,548 --> 00:27:25,746
I just wanted to help.

560
00:27:25,746 --> 00:27:26,538
I didn’t mean to meddle.

561
00:27:27,151 --> 00:27:28,033
Why would you help me?

562
00:27:28,792 --> 00:27:30,229
You helped me yesterday.

563
00:27:30,536 --> 00:27:32,070
Today, I wanted to help you too.

564
00:27:34,443 --> 00:27:37,242
Is there anything else I can help you with?

565
00:27:51,534 --> 00:27:52,541
Sea Clean.

566
00:27:52,541 --> 00:27:53,210
P’Niran.

567
00:27:53,388 --> 00:27:53,985
What?

568
00:27:54,420 --> 00:27:55,084
Huh?

569
00:27:55,294 --> 00:27:56,016
Hey.

570
00:27:56,936 --> 00:27:58,191
How do you know my name?

571
00:27:58,288 --> 00:27:59,047
Did you spy on me?

572
00:28:00,968 --> 00:28:02,193
Ah.

573
00:28:03,662 --> 00:28:04,723
I must be famous.

574
00:28:05,353 --> 00:28:06,602
My name is Cheewa.

575
00:28:06,763 --> 00:28:08,358
Or you can call me Parncheewa.

576
00:28:08,600 --> 00:28:09,895
But Parncheewa is longer.

577
00:28:10,089 --> 00:28:10,979
It’s up to you.

578
00:28:11,448 --> 00:28:12,848
You can call me anything.

579
00:28:14,930 --> 00:28:17,460
Then can I call you Glasses?

580
00:28:17,541 --> 00:28:18,340
No.

581
00:28:18,340 --> 00:28:19,162
My name is not Glasses.

582
00:28:20,340 --> 00:28:22,925
Glasses are the object Parncheewa wears.

583
00:28:27,961 --> 00:28:28,689
Right.

584
00:28:28,802 --> 00:28:30,137
Gravity Junior.

585
00:28:35,595 --> 00:28:37,893
If you want to use gravity on me again,
you can.

586
00:28:40,121 --> 00:28:41,628
But I have to go to class now.

587
00:28:43,210 --> 00:28:44,396
Once school’s over,

588
00:28:46,511 --> 00:28:47,669
you can.

589
00:28:48,589 --> 00:28:49,171
Huh?

590
00:28:51,431 --> 00:28:52,098
Oh?

591
00:28:53,745 --> 00:28:54,707
What’s wrong with him?

592
00:28:54,707 --> 00:28:55,443
Leaving just like that.

593
00:29:00,441 --> 00:29:01,482
P’Niran.

594
00:29:04,388 --> 00:29:07,724
Please read the details in the brochure.

595
00:29:08,095 --> 00:29:11,401
If you’re interested,
come to the Astronomy Club.

596
00:29:12,031 --> 00:29:12,912
Top floor.

597
00:29:12,912 --> 00:29:13,569
Science building.

598
00:29:13,746 --> 00:29:16,242
I’m always there when I’m not in class.

599
00:29:16,888 --> 00:29:17,519
Wait.

600
00:29:18,084 --> 00:29:19,396
How would I know your timetable?

601
00:29:19,590 --> 00:29:21,719
I can send it to you later.

602
00:29:31,165 --> 00:29:34,046
You know Cheewa?

603
00:29:35,547 --> 00:29:36,634
Are you guys close?

604
00:29:37,651 --> 00:29:38,746
That kid with the glasses?

605
00:29:39,311 --> 00:29:40,021
Hey.

606
00:29:40,683 --> 00:29:41,521
I think they went that way.

607
00:29:48,009 --> 00:29:48,838
Idiots.

608
00:29:49,403 --> 00:29:50,495
Blind as hell.

609
00:29:53,210 --> 00:29:54,075
You’re…

610
00:29:54,947 --> 00:29:56,414
the guy who sat on my lap.

611
00:29:57,609 --> 00:29:58,337
Don’t be ridiculous.

612
00:29:58,757 --> 00:30:00,029
I didn’t want to sit on your lap.

613
00:30:01,498 --> 00:30:02,378
Sorry.

614
00:30:07,318 --> 00:30:09,957
You saved me. Thank you.

615
00:30:17,308 --> 00:30:18,962
You’re pretty kind.

616
00:30:20,996 --> 00:30:22,152
Gravity Senior.

617
00:30:24,089 --> 00:30:25,286
My name is not Gravity.

618
00:30:25,803 --> 00:30:26,944
Then what’s your name?

619
00:30:30,302 --> 00:30:31,074
I’m not telling you.

620
00:30:31,784 --> 00:30:32,639
You don’t need to know.

621
00:30:32,639 --> 00:30:33,549
We’re not close.

622
00:30:34,727 --> 00:30:37,047
I know the names of a lot of planets.

623
00:30:40,130 --> 00:30:41,817
And I’m not close to any of them.

624
00:30:45,698 --> 00:30:46,602
You’re just…

625
00:30:49,201 --> 00:30:50,934
Ugh, never mind.
I don’t want to talk to you anymore.

626
00:30:59,009 --> 00:30:59,647
Glasses.

627
00:31:00,841 --> 00:31:01,553
Yes?

628
00:31:09,196 --> 00:31:10,129
You should hurry home.

629
00:31:10,290 --> 00:31:11,488
Or you’ll get your money taken again.

630
00:31:14,926 --> 00:31:15,523
Hey.

631
00:31:17,961 --> 00:31:19,957
Can you walk me out?

632
00:31:20,506 --> 00:31:21,139
Huh?

633
00:31:21,930 --> 00:31:23,005
What are you doing here, boys?

634
00:31:23,005 --> 00:31:23,692
To…

635
00:31:23,692 --> 00:31:25,839
Do you know
how old the universe is?

636
00:31:25,839 --> 00:31:27,383
Once you learn more about something,

637
00:31:27,544 --> 00:31:28,856
you’ll feel even closer to it.

638
00:31:28,856 --> 00:31:30,186
Are you shy watching me change?

639
00:31:30,299 --> 00:31:31,609
Why don’t you change in the restroom?

640
00:31:42,493 --> 00:31:44,237
Can you walk me out?

641
00:31:44,947 --> 00:31:45,591
Huh?

642
00:31:47,404 --> 00:31:48,317
Are you out of your mind?

643
00:31:49,289 --> 00:31:50,147
We’re not close.

644
00:31:50,147 --> 00:31:50,858
We barely know each other.

645
00:31:50,858 --> 00:31:51,669
And you want me to walk you out?

646
00:31:51,837 --> 00:31:52,401
You’re crazy.

647
00:31:54,139 --> 00:31:55,013
Just go.

648
00:31:55,013 --> 00:31:55,953
They’re not following you anymore.

649
00:31:56,961 --> 00:31:58,466
Go on ahead.

650
00:31:59,326 --> 00:32:00,238
I’ll keep an eye out for you.

651
00:32:05,059 --> 00:32:05,894
Go home.

652
00:32:07,352 --> 00:32:08,205
Which way?

653
00:32:08,411 --> 00:32:09,300
That way!

654
00:32:10,159 --> 00:32:11,676
Do you want to follow them?

655
00:32:13,863 --> 00:32:15,255
Aren’t you going to walk me out?

656
00:32:17,778 --> 00:32:19,434
Seriously? Want me to throw you?

657
00:32:20,574 --> 00:32:21,249
No.

658
00:32:21,324 --> 00:32:21,830
Right.

659
00:32:27,117 --> 00:32:27,792
Look at him.

660
00:32:29,474 --> 00:32:30,149
Ugh.

661
00:32:34,204 --> 00:32:35,701
What? Hurry up!

662
00:32:36,961 --> 00:32:37,543
Left!

663
00:32:39,169 --> 00:32:40,426
Did you see me talk to him?

664
00:32:42,108 --> 00:32:42,853
Yeah.

665
00:32:42,853 --> 00:32:44,338
Exactly. We’ve talked before.

666
00:32:45,553 --> 00:32:46,562
What a dumb question.

667
00:32:48,207 --> 00:32:49,522
No, I’m going that way!

668
00:32:49,896 --> 00:32:51,600
Wanna get punched?

669
00:32:55,076 --> 00:32:56,454
Are you sure, Niran?

670
00:32:56,790 --> 00:32:57,856
It’s astronomy.

671
00:32:58,379 --> 00:33:00,063
I only know Planet Namek.

672
00:33:00,792 --> 00:33:02,341
I need to get my activity hours.

673
00:33:02,341 --> 00:33:04,106
Otherwise, I won’t graduate with you guys.

674
00:33:04,424 --> 00:33:06,412
Come on. Can’t you just join me?

675
00:33:10,696 --> 00:33:12,235
What are you doing here, boys?

676
00:33:12,795 --> 00:33:14,512
To… sign up for

677
00:33:14,512 --> 00:33:16,588
the Astronomy Club’s Volunteer Camp.

678
00:33:16,588 --> 00:33:17,564
Oh!

679
00:33:18,312 --> 00:33:20,099
Welcome!

680
00:33:20,641 --> 00:33:21,364
Oh!

681
00:33:24,093 --> 00:33:24,826
Great!

682
00:33:25,293 --> 00:33:26,639
Come on in! Welcome!

683
00:33:26,639 --> 00:33:28,269
You guys made the right choice.

684
00:33:28,269 --> 00:33:29,859
Our club is happy to have you.

685
00:33:30,009 --> 00:33:31,342
Are you into astronomy?

686
00:33:32,725 --> 00:33:33,620
Did you know

687
00:33:33,620 --> 00:33:38,845
that astronomy and the universe
are actually much closer to us than we think?

688
00:33:40,191 --> 00:33:41,107
Closer to us?

689
00:33:41,238 --> 00:33:42,338
Of course.

690
00:33:42,880 --> 00:33:45,315
You may feel that it’s so vast and far away,

691
00:33:45,315 --> 00:33:49,529
but actually, we’re part of it.

692
00:33:51,873 --> 00:33:53,142
Do you know

693
00:33:53,310 --> 00:33:57,160
how long it would take
to explore the universe?

694
00:34:01,961 --> 00:34:02,877
No, I don’t.

695
00:34:02,877 --> 00:34:03,708
Correct.

696
00:34:03,708 --> 00:34:04,208
Oh?

697
00:34:04,208 --> 00:34:05,535
I don’t know either.

698
00:34:05,535 --> 00:34:08,002
That’s why we’re learning here.

699
00:34:08,563 --> 00:34:09,297
Come on in.

700
00:34:09,297 --> 00:34:10,187
We’re having fun.

701
00:34:12,523 --> 00:34:13,128
Come on.

702
00:34:13,128 --> 00:34:14,145
Oh, okay.

703
00:34:15,079 --> 00:34:17,174
Hey, come greet our new friends.

704
00:34:18,482 --> 00:34:19,770
I’ve been waiting for you.

705
00:34:31,027 --> 00:34:31,800
See?

706
00:34:32,774 --> 00:34:34,689
This one goes up like this.

707
00:34:37,623 --> 00:34:40,032
Do people from outside the club
usually not join in?

708
00:34:41,602 --> 00:34:42,668
Not really.

709
00:34:54,188 --> 00:34:56,398
Do you know how old the universe is?

710
00:34:57,127 --> 00:34:57,825
No.

711
00:34:58,031 --> 00:34:59,006
Who would know?

712
00:35:00,165 --> 00:35:01,884
Almost 14 billion years old.

713
00:35:02,482 --> 00:35:03,299
Whoa.

714
00:35:04,455 --> 00:35:06,302
14 thousand…

715
00:35:06,844 --> 00:35:07,756
Zero.

716
00:35:08,195 --> 00:35:09,266
Six.

717
00:35:10,959 --> 00:35:11,459
Zeros.

718
00:35:15,458 --> 00:35:18,095
Eight. Nine. Ten.

719
00:35:19,403 --> 00:35:20,674
That’s one too many.

720
00:35:21,793 --> 00:35:23,030
There are nine zeros.

721
00:35:25,553 --> 00:35:27,555
It’s really old, huh?

722
00:35:28,586 --> 00:35:29,086
Yes.

723
00:35:29,591 --> 00:35:31,480
That’s why there are so many things
I want to know.

724
00:35:33,629 --> 00:35:34,776
Are you into older people?

725
00:35:37,224 --> 00:35:39,236
Maybe not that much older.

726
00:35:40,768 --> 00:35:42,361
Once you learn more about something,

727
00:35:43,520 --> 00:35:44,942
you’ll feel even closer to it.

728
00:35:47,540 --> 00:35:48,585
Even closer.

729
00:35:53,463 --> 00:35:54,855
And did you know

730
00:35:55,939 --> 00:35:59,397
the stars we see might not exist
in the present?

731
00:36:01,527 --> 00:36:03,820
It can take years for the light to reach us.

732
00:36:05,278 --> 00:36:06,522
Or even millions of years.

733
00:36:07,886 --> 00:36:08,770
What we see

734
00:36:12,956 --> 00:36:14,957
might be from the past.

735
00:36:36,367 --> 00:36:37,650
Stop it, Thara!

736
00:36:38,416 --> 00:36:40,049
Your saliva is all over my shirt!

737
00:36:40,049 --> 00:36:40,666
What the hell?

738
00:36:41,432 --> 00:36:42,417
What?

739
00:36:44,061 --> 00:36:46,473
Ew!

740
00:36:53,743 --> 00:36:55,624
Why do you have a student shirt
in your bag?

741
00:36:55,774 --> 00:36:56,987
And other shirts too.

742
00:36:58,819 --> 00:37:00,421
I have everything in my bag.

743
00:37:04,626 --> 00:37:06,367
Do you have mosquito repellent?

744
00:37:08,086 --> 00:37:09,482
I have mosquito spray.

745
00:37:10,117 --> 00:37:10,756
Just a second.

746
00:37:10,756 --> 00:37:12,175
Stop. I’m just kidding.

747
00:37:14,916 --> 00:37:16,596
Please go and change into my shirt.

748
00:37:17,119 --> 00:37:19,320
You said you couldn’t stand
the smell of P’Thara’s saliva.

749
00:37:25,282 --> 00:37:26,878
Why don’t you change in the restroom?

750
00:37:28,915 --> 00:37:31,182
I’m just changing, not taking a shower.

751
00:37:32,528 --> 00:37:33,152
Why?

752
00:37:33,339 --> 00:37:34,584
Are you shy watching me change?

753
00:37:38,857 --> 00:37:40,348
Hurry up.

754
00:37:41,694 --> 00:37:42,870
Stop talking.

755
00:37:44,533 --> 00:37:46,161
Just take off your glasses
if you don’t want to see.

756
00:37:49,020 --> 00:37:50,078
No.

757
00:37:50,433 --> 00:37:51,683
It’ll be hard for me to see.

758
00:37:51,961 --> 00:37:53,599
It won’t be that hard.

759
00:37:54,720 --> 00:37:55,425
Huh, Glasses?

760
00:37:57,313 --> 00:37:57,995
How do you say it?

761
00:37:58,649 --> 00:38:01,748
Just let gravity guide you.

762
00:38:02,327 --> 00:38:02,901
Right?

763
00:38:04,004 --> 00:38:06,240
Knowledge doesn't really sink in with you, does it?

764
00:38:07,174 --> 00:38:09,264
Please hurry up and finish changing.

765
00:38:09,769 --> 00:38:11,742
There’s no point in rambling.

766
00:38:12,247 --> 00:38:14,516
I was listening to you ramble just now.

767
00:38:15,245 --> 00:38:15,965
Fine.

768
00:38:17,684 --> 00:38:19,143
So which one do you want?

769
00:38:22,899 --> 00:38:23,561
This one.

770
00:38:24,981 --> 00:38:27,455
No, I’m wearing it.

771
00:38:27,455 --> 00:38:28,069
Take it off for me.

772
00:38:29,284 --> 00:38:30,425
They’re the same.

773
00:38:30,425 --> 00:38:31,602
Just wear that one.

774
00:38:33,620 --> 00:38:34,756
Come here. Take it off.

775
00:38:38,456 --> 00:38:39,980
So which one do you want?

776
00:38:47,181 --> 00:38:48,975
That Cheewa kid is nice.

777
00:38:49,181 --> 00:38:50,635
He even had a spare shirt for you to borrow.

778
00:38:51,121 --> 00:38:53,287
Shut up. Wash my shirt.

779
00:38:53,399 --> 00:38:54,835
Yeah. I’m going now.

780
00:38:54,835 --> 00:38:55,340
See you.

781
00:39:30,560 --> 00:39:32,096
Really? We live near each other?

782
00:39:32,824 --> 00:39:33,617
That’s right.

783
00:39:37,186 --> 00:39:38,289
Are you talking to me?

784
00:39:38,532 --> 00:39:39,281
Yes.

785
00:39:40,216 --> 00:39:41,553
Why didn’t you turn around to talk to me?

786
00:39:42,282 --> 00:39:44,564
You didn’t seem like you wanted to talk to me on the bus.

787
00:39:44,770 --> 00:39:46,130
So I pretended I didn’t see you.

788
00:39:47,550 --> 00:39:48,429
It’s not like that.

789
00:39:48,541 --> 00:39:49,212
It’s just…

790
00:39:50,165 --> 00:39:51,882
I mean, we’re not close.
What do you want me to say?

791
00:39:53,770 --> 00:39:54,955
Anything.

792
00:39:57,459 --> 00:39:58,091
But…

793
00:40:00,745 --> 00:40:03,259
I don’t even know
any of the planets you’re into.

794
00:40:05,352 --> 00:40:07,261
I’m not just into planets.

795
00:40:11,204 --> 00:40:13,106
Oh… really?

796
00:40:16,078 --> 00:40:17,500
I’m into you, too.

797
00:40:23,212 --> 00:40:25,557
Are you into anyone, P’Niran?

798
00:40:33,810 --> 00:40:36,270
I want to get to know you better.

799
00:40:40,384 --> 00:40:41,789
Can I hit on you?

800
00:40:52,209 --> 00:40:52,802
Hold on.

801
00:40:52,802 --> 00:40:53,650
It felt like the world stopped turning for a second.

802
00:40:53,650 --> 00:40:55,372
Are you still worried about Auntie Tang?

803
00:40:55,372 --> 00:40:58,649
Let’s come up with a plan
to win those customers back for her.

804
00:40:58,649 --> 00:41:00,833
What are the seniors from the Music Club doing?

805
00:41:00,833 --> 00:41:02,681
Whoever buys food from Auntie Tang today,

806
00:41:02,681 --> 00:41:03,696
gets a free hug.

807
00:41:03,696 --> 00:41:04,998
I’m here for a free hug.

808
00:41:04,998 --> 00:41:05,845
You don’t have to do this.

809
00:41:05,845 --> 00:41:06,961
No one’s forcing you.

810
00:41:07,167 --> 00:41:09,100
I’m just claiming what I’m entitled to.

811
00:41:09,100 --> 00:41:12,311
This means I’m another step closer
to winning you over, P’Niran.

812
00:41:12,685 --> 00:41:14,284
Tell me honestly.

813
00:41:14,284 --> 00:41:16,785
Aren’t you shy at all?

814
00:41:17,533 --> 00:41:19,996
What’s wrong? Are you shy?

815
00:41:20,089 --> 00:41:21,316
Why are you smiling so much?

816
00:41:21,316 --> 00:41:23,123
Someday, you’ll smile at me like this.

817
00:41:23,403 --> 00:41:25,679
After the match, I have a reward for you.

818
00:41:25,679 --> 00:41:28,394
This is what happens when you miss practice.

819
00:41:28,394 --> 00:41:31,488
No one deserves to be scolded for losing a sports competition, P’Niran.

820
00:41:31,488 --> 00:41:33,424
Are you sad that you lost?

821
00:41:33,424 --> 00:41:34,117
Of course.

822
00:41:34,117 --> 00:41:36,621
I guess you won’t get to reward me, then.

823
00:41:36,621 --> 00:41:37,811
I lost.

824
00:41:37,811 --> 00:41:40,115
I was going to give you a gift anyway.
